      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I went ahead and tried going back to Live, running the game, and then going back to the Open Beta. The issue did not happen again, but I also noticed when I went back on Live that the files Steam failed to delete before weren't there. That leads me to believe that they may have been some left overs from some previous version of Live that eventually went unused, and Steam decided to leave them out of the uninstallation process at some point causing the Open Beta to try and use files from an older version of Unity, causing the error. That's the only conclusion I can think of anyway.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
